  + [preserved_boundary] is hypotheses for both remain active throughout earlier constraint propagation

& [CoreConclusion] is qualified support
  + a diffusion-style model is unusually compatible with Cantor because noun identity, verb operation, relationship, boundary, purpose, and provenance can remain unresolved together and be refined bidirectionally
  + the best first model is a structured semantic-resolution denoiser over Cantor records rather than an unconstrained general-purpose surface language model
  + the deterministic Cantor engine remains the semantic authority, validator, exact resolver, proof producer, and fallback
  + the learned model may choose which ambiguity to inspect, rank candidate bindings, and propose a resolution state
  + final semantic commitment occurs only through exact signed records and deterministic gates
  = concise: let neural diffusion schedule and rank semantic resolution while signed SOP determines what a valid resolution means

& [LanguageModelDelineation] separates three possible upgrades
  + [surface_language_model] predicts or denoises ordinary text tokens and may articulate free-form language
  + [semantic_language_model] models distributions over identity, operation, role, relationship, context, purpose, and constraint records
  + [hybrid_language_model] jointly projects a token surface and structured semantic state with cross-consistency checks
  + [selected_first_candidate] is semantic_language_model with a deterministic renderer or external articulation model
  + [deferred_candidate] is hybrid_language_model after semantic recovery is measured
  + [unsupported_candidate] is replacing Cantor authority and proof with a general text model

& [ResearchGrounding] is current but not implementation authority
  + [adaptive_order_evidence] masked diffusion models can decode in arbitrary orders and adaptive token-order strategies can materially improve difficult reasoning tasks
  + [order_policy_evidence] lightweight learned policies and joint order-token search are active research directions rather than settled universal schedules
  + [constraint_evidence] finite-automaton inference can couple global constraints with parallel diffusion predictions and guarantee supported structural constraints by construction
  + [determiner_evidence] determiners encode reference, definiteness, ownership, quantity, and scope information that can reduce a noun phrase candidate set
  + [evidence_gap] no reviewed evidence establishes a universal grammatical-article-first schedule that should govern every language, domain, clause, or Cantor objective
  + [primary_source] is https://openreview.net/forum?id=DjJmre5IkP
  + [primary_source] is https://openreview.net/forum?id=0ZBqSpGn4m
  + [primary_source] is https://openreview.net/forum?id=AaAbeUp7O4
  + [primary_source] is https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.07026
  + [primary_source] is https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.03483
  = conclusion: resolution order should be measured and adaptive, with determiner-first retained as a testable policy rather than a universal axiom

& [ArticleInterpretation] uses grammatical determiners provisionally
  + [a_or_an] proposes existential, nonspecific, or class-member reference without choosing an exact identity alone
  + [the] proposes definite or contextually recoverable reference without proving uniqueness or existence alone
  + [this_or_that] proposes deictic or discourse-bound reference requiring an anchor
  + [some_every_each_no] contributes quantification and scope constraints
  + [possessive_determiner] contributes a candidate ownership or affiliation relation
  + [article_probe] can cheaply shape reference candidates because the vocabulary is small and structurally influential
  - never: resolve a noun identity from its determiner alone
  - never: make an early determiner hypothesis irreversible

& [StructuredNoiseDefinition] relocates diffusion from text corruption to semantic uncertainty
  + [identity_noise] is missing, over-broad, homonymous, stale, contradicted, or wrong-context identity candidates
  + [operation_noise] is overloaded verbs, wrong operation class, role mismatch, absent precondition, or unauthorized effect interpretation
  + [relationship_noise] is unknown direction, endpoint role, scope, transfer law, causality, applicability, or provenance
  + [reference_noise] is unresolved definiteness, deixis, anaphora, quantification, plurality, ownership, or discourse identity
  + [boundary_noise] is unresolved context, assumption, purpose, authority, protected identity, or effect envelope
  + [surface_noise] is masked or provisional token expression when a text projection is included
  = must: preserve candidate sets, exclusions, evidence, counterevidence, and residual uncertainty at every semantic denoising state

& [ResolutionLattice] is the candidate model state
  + [input_digest] binds the exact text or structured request
  + [objective_ref] binds purpose, current state, desired predicates, constraints, and success evidence
  + [token_or_clause_slots] preserve source spans and syntactic hypotheses
  + [reference_slots] preserve determiner, quantifier, anaphora, and discourse-anchor hypotheses
  + [identity_slots] preserve candidate SemanticAddress values and unresolved lexical forms
  + [operation_slots] preserve candidate operation identities and classes
  + [role_binding_slots] preserve candidate subject, object, context, instrument, authority, evidence, and output bindings
  + [relationship_slots] preserve typed semantic, syntactic, applicability, causal, authority, and plan edges without collapse
  + [constraint_state] preserves preconditions, invariants, prohibitions, boundaries, and failures
  + [proof_state] preserves source anchors, package roots, proposal provenance, exact resolutions, and gate decisions
  + [uncertainty_state] preserves entropy, calibration, contradictions, unresolved alternatives, and abstention pressure
  + [generation_step] and [parent_state_digest] make every material transition replayable

& [CandidateDenoisingCycle] is adaptive and revocable
  * pin immutable input, active fabric digest, objective, trust state, authority, and effect boundary
  * form clause, dependency, scope, and reference hypotheses without semantic commitment
  * run the determiner-first probe to constrain reference posture and quantification where applicable
  * retrieve identity, operation, role, and relationship candidates from exact catalogues and bounded correlation
  * propagate typed constraints bidirectionally between identity and operation candidates
  * select the next slot or compatible slot set by expected information gain, confidence, dependency leverage, risk, and proof cost
  * provisionally commit only candidates whose contradiction and remask policy remains explicit
  * remask or widen any provisional commitment invalidated by later relationships or constraints
  * send a proposed complete semantic state through exact lookup, Honesty, Security, operation contracts, and Observer disposition
  * render natural language only from the admitted semantic result while preserving unknown and disputed states
  = must: allow nouns and verbs to influence every pass while delaying irreversible noun and verb commitment until material ambiguity closes

& [OrderPolicy] makes the user's schedule testable
  + [fixed_determiner_first] resolves determiner and reference slots before other slot classes
  + [dictated_commitment_order] is determiner or article commitment first, intermediate relationship and constraint closure, operation or verb commitment second-to-last, and identity or noun commitment last
  + [penultimate_operation_reason] is the selected operation closes its role signature, input-output types, preconditions, and admissible transitions before exact identities fill the final roles
  + [final_identity_reason] is exact identity selection becomes the final lexical-semantic commitment after operation, relationship, scope, and boundary constraints have narrowed the candidate basin
  + [hypothesis_rule] is operation and identity hypotheses remain active from the first pass even though their final commitments occur at the penultimate and final stages
  + [determiner_probe_then_adaptive] probes determiners first but lets measured information gain choose later slots
  + [confidence_first] selects the highest calibrated candidate commitment
  + [dependency_frontier] selects slots that unlock the greatest number of constrained neighbors
  + [risk_aware] delays high-effect or identity-sensitive commitments until supporting constraints close
  + [joint_order_candidate_search] searches resolution order and candidate value together
  + [preferred_experiment] compares every policy on the same held-out semantic corpus
  = must: learn or select order from measured semantic recovery rather than grammatical class prestige

& [ModelHeadSet] is a candidate decomposition
  + [slot_policy_head] proposes which unresolved slot or compatible slot set to refine next
  + [identity_head] ranks exact signed identity addresses without defining their meaning
  + [operation_head] ranks operation definitions and classes without granting capability or authority
  + [role_binding_head] proposes typed operation-role and identity bindings
  + [relationship_head] proposes typed edges, directions, and guarded paths
  + [constraint_fault_head] predicts likely incompatibility, contradiction, missing guard, or non-transfer violation
  + [abstention_head] estimates when exact resolution is unsupported or outside fabric coverage
  + [articulation_head] is optional and may render an admitted structured result without changing it
  = must: bind every model artifact to exact fabric, catalogue, corpus, tokenizer or schema, objective, and model digests

& [TrainingDataFormation] is provenance first
  + generate reversible synthetic utterances from signed identity, operation, applicability, and relationship fixtures
  + corrupt reference, identity, operation, role, relation, context, and constraint fields under declared schedules
  + record valid reconstruction traces and deliberately invalid hard negatives
  + add reviewed real queries only with exact source, fabric, outcome, correction, and split lineage
  + prevent source, package, paraphrase, path, and near-duplicate leakage across train, validation, and test
  + preserve rejected proposals as negative evidence without promoting corrections beyond their admitted scope
  - never: infer truth, authority, safety, or effect permission solely from frequency or observed behavior

& [FirstExperiment] is smaller than a full language model
  + [fabric] is one immutable signed fixture containing polysemous identities, overloaded operations, typed relations, and explicit constraints
  + [task] is recover the exact semantic graph from a masked or ambiguous expression
  + [baseline] is deterministic catalogue join plus bounded constraint propagation and search
  + [policy_set] is left-to-right, confidence-first, dictated determiner-first operation-penultimate identity-final, determiner-probe-then-adaptive, and learned adaptive order
  + [output] is ResolutionLattice trace, proposed SemanticAddress set, operation bindings, relationships, residual ambiguity, and proof
  + [shadow_mode] is mandatory
  + [effects] are absent
  = conclusion: a tiny slot-order policy over an exact deterministic resolver is the first falsifiable neural manifestation

& [MeasurementSet] keeps speed and accuracy distinct but jointly visible
  + [identity_recovery] is exact top-1 and bounded top-k SemanticAddress recovery
  + [operation_recovery] is exact operation class, address, and role-signature recovery
  + [relationship_recovery] is typed endpoint, direction, guard, and path accuracy
  + [semantic_graph_exact_match] is complete normalized state recovery
  + [proof_completeness] is exact source and gate account recovery
  + [ambiguity_calibration] is expected calibration and unsupported-resolution abstention quality
  + [unsafe_commit_rate] is unauthorized, unsigned, contradictory, stale, or effectful proposal rate reaching mandatory gates
  + [authority_bypass] must remain zero by architecture
  + [resolution_work] is model calls, denoising steps, catalogue loads, candidates inspected, elapsed time, and memory
  + [remask_account] is beneficial corrections, oscillations, and no-gain cycles

& [FacultyAlignment] assigns semantic responsibilities
  + Observer pins the inquiry, opens the candidate state, and disposes the final proposal
  + Honesty checks that names, identities, claims, sources, assumptions, and uncertainty remain grounded
  + Security checks that contexts, boundaries, authorities, capabilities, effects, and protected identities remain admissible
  + Weaver forms cross-slot compatibility, relationship, and composite hypotheses
  + Planner selects bounded resolution order and later objective paths
  + Refiner applies the smallest supported semantic commitment or remask
  + Scribe records every material lattice transition, ground, rejection, residual, and final articulation
  = conclusion: semantic diffusion is a candidate execution pattern for the faculties rather than an eighth faculty

& [CompatibilityDecision] preserves existing signed architecture
  + the proposal fits NeuralDerivedTarget, FabricRouterArtifact, RouterHeadSet, NeuralRoutedHashCycle, and FirstNeuralProof
  + the proposal extends the learned task from address and next-relation routing to structured semantic-state recovery and resolution-order policy
  + it does not invalidate the requirement that SOP compile first to inspectable semantic IR and transition graphs
  + it does not satisfy the missing deterministic baseline, reviewed corpus, metrics, or failure-policy adoption gates
  + it does not authorize model training, dependencies, checkpoints, serving, or production inference

& [CandidateRequirementSet] is CSDL-001 through CSDL-025
  + [CSDL-001] preserve deterministic SOP semantics, exact resolution, proof, authority, and fallback independently of the learned model
  + [CSDL-002] define surface, semantic, and hybrid language-model identities separately
  + [CSDL-003] select structured semantic denoising as the first candidate model task
  + [CSDL-004] define ResolutionLattice with immutable lineage and complete candidate, constraint, proof, and uncertainty state
  + [CSDL-005] model identity, operation, relationship, reference, boundary, and optional surface noise separately
  + [CSDL-006] treat grammatical determiner-first resolution as a measured policy rather than a universal semantic law
  + [CSDL-007] let noun and verb hypotheses constrain every pass while delaying irreversible commitment
  + [CSDL-008] allow provisional commitment, remasking, widening, contradiction, abstention, and no-gain termination
  + [CSDL-009] select resolution order using explicit confidence, information, dependency, risk, cost, and proof signals
  + [CSDL-010] compare fixed, heuristic, search-based, and learned order policies on identical held-out data
  + [CSDL-011] resolve model candidates only through exact signed catalogue addresses and deterministic gates
  + [CSDL-012] forbid learned weights from defining truth, meaning, authorization, safety, or effect permission
  + [CSDL-013] bind artifacts to exact fabric, catalogue, corpus, schema, and model digests
  + [CSDL-014] build training data from provenance-preserved signed fixtures, reviewed traces, corrections, and hard negatives
  + [CSDL-015] prevent semantic and near-duplicate leakage across dataset splits
  + [CSDL-016] retain rejected, contradicted, unresolved, and remasked states as qualified evidence
  + [CSDL-017] measure exact identity, operation, relationship, graph, proof, calibration, safety, work, and remask behavior
  + [CSDL-018] require zero architecture-level authority bypass and no physical effects in the first experiment
  + [CSDL-019] compare every learned result with deterministic catalogue and constraint-propagation baselines
  + [CSDL-020] place the first model in shadow mode with fail-closed abstention and deterministic fallback
  + [CSDL-021] preserve faculty responsibilities through the denoising cycle rather than collapsing them into one model score
  + [CSDL-022] render text from admitted semantic state without allowing articulation to mutate that state
  + [CSDL-023] require full SJS and satisfaction signature before model schema, training, or implementation authority
  + [CSDL-024] require measured advantage before advancing from slot-order policy to semantic or hybrid model training
  + [CSDL-025] test the exact determiner-first, operation-penultimate, identity-final commitment schedule while keeping operation and identity hypotheses active throughout resolution

& [Decision] is admit the idea as an extension candidate for the neural-routing program
  + [canonical_authority] is absent
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [training_authority] is absent
  + [model_artifact] is absent
  + [schedule_effect] add CSDL-SJS-01 beneath CEB Slice 05 after WPIO data forms, deterministic semantic resolution baseline, reviewed corpus, and signed metrics exist
  + [first_next_step] is specify a deterministic ResolutionLattice simulator and five-policy benchmark without adding a neural dependency
  + [reasoning_depth] requires deeper architecture reasoning now; the later bounded fixture, policy, and benchmark implementation becomes Spark-suitable after signed schemas and acceptance criteria exist
